<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss govt to allow gene-altered soy imports.</title>
<headline>Swiss govt to allow gene-altered soy imports.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE, Switzerland 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss Federal Department of Domestic Affairs (EDI) said it rejected an appeal to ban imports of food products containing gene-altered soy, and said such products could be imported immediately.</p>
<p>&quot;Food products containing gene-altered soy can be immediately imported into Switzerland and brought onto the market,&quot; the EDI said in a statement.</p>
<p>The decision has implications for U.S. firm Monsanto Co, which developed a strain of gene-altered soy, and also for Swiss chocolate manufacturers, now banned from using lecithin containing gene-altered soy in their products.</p>
</text>
